<Base title="Research"><section class="page-title narrow"><div class="eyebrow">Research agenda</div><h1>Making distributed AI systems faster, more efficient and easier to operate.</h1><p class="lead">My interests sit at the boundary between computer systems, distributed computing and machine learning infrastructure.</p></section><section class="prose narrow"><h2>Efficient LLM inference</h2><p>Weight transfer and model restoration, inference-serving latency, scheduling, memory pressure and the interaction of accelerator communication with compute.</p><p>On Ascend NPUs, I investigated safetensors-aware tensor organization and huge-page-backed HBM allocation for reducing time per output token (TPOT). <a href="/projects/ascend-tpot/">Read the technical brief ↗</a></p><h2>GPU/NPU runtime systems</h2><p>Data paths between CPU memory and accelerators, topology-aware transfer, asynchronous execution and performance characterisation.</p><h2>Distributed resource management</h2><p>Distributed runtimes, cloud and edge placement, multi-tenant scheduling and operational design for AI platforms.</p><h2>Research methodology</h2><p>End-to-end prototype development, hardware-level measurement, systems benchmarking and comparison against practical baselines.</p></section></Base>
